{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/776699-solar-brawl-athetlics-suggestions","id":776699,"title":"Solar Brawl/Athetlics Suggestions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-29T11:37:19-08:00","id":776699,"title":"Solar Brawl/Athetlics Suggestions?","content":"I got invited to a 3E game, and after watching too much One Punch Man I wanna play a Supernal Brawl Dawn with favored Athletics. Any suggestions on charms with a good synergy? I have little experience with Solar attack charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8946-lonesome-akuma","name":"Lonesome Akuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T11:49:11-08:00","id":776705,"title":"","content":"Thunderclap Rush Attack + Thunderbolt Attack Prana + Heaven Thunder Hammer* gives a nice feeling of a ridiculously fast movement with a ridiculously strong punch at the end of it. You can add more stuff to that setup to pump damage to truly murderous heights, such as Burning Fist Burial and Adamantine Fists of Battle.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:9px\"> I also like that the names of the Charms happen to go well thematically. Might as well call this combo the Thunder Trifecta or something like that XD</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 11-29-2015, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T11:52:22-08:00","id":776707,"title":"","content":"There's a couple of early charms you'll want from Brawl. One gives your foe a persistent Onslaught penalty, and I think one raises your Withering damage by the level of their Onslaught. Those two in combination are GREAT for pummeling the fuck out of your foes, and setting up for a good Heaven Thunder Hammer. Which will never STOP being fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:06:18-08:00","id":776718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/776699-solar-brawl-athetlics-suggestions?p=776707#post776707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a couple of early charms you'll want from Brawl. One gives your foe a persistent Onslaught penalty, and I think one raises your Withering damage by the level of their Onslaught. Those two in combination are GREAT for pummeling the fuck out of your foes, and setting up for a good Heaven Thunder Hammer. Which will never STOP being fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Unlike Saitama you won't be able to always win in one punch, so the onslaught setup is really good for prolonged battles. Also, Wind and Stones defense, so you can use that Onslaught penalty to increase you defenses too.<br /> <br /> So. From Atlhetics: Monkey Leap Technique, Increasing Strength Exercise and Thunderbolt Attack Prana (lightning speed is also in theme for a Saitama-based character, if you can spare another Charm). From Brawl: Thunderclap Rush Attack, Falling Hammer Strike, Ferocious Jab, Wind and Stones Defense, Heaven Thunder Hammer.<br /> <br /> Observe that this is all Essence 1, though. If you don't want to go for the likes of Adamantine/Orichalcum fists of Battle or the bunch of Charms you need for Super Saya...I mean, Ascendant Battle Visage, you may want to consider taking Resistance as your Supernal, so you can no-sell stuff with Adamant Skin Technique and Aegis of Invincible Might.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:15:15-08:00","id":776727,"title":"","content":"I don't know this show your talking about, but I assume its all about dropping people with a single punch. Here is a break down of the stuff to grab, as a basic suite of bad ass punching. You should be aware that artifact heavy armor can screw this up due to Hardness. <br /> <br /> Brawl: I assume your not interested in grapples...<br /> -Heaven Thunder Hammer, &amp; Thunderclap Rush Attack are always useful for the offense, for the defense I would suggest Wind &amp; Stones Strike used with Falling Hammer Strike for the Withering Defense but vs. decisive attacks Force Rending Strike is MUCH more likely to work. <br /> <br /> Athletics charms<br /> -Increasing Strength Exercise, Lightning Speed, &amp; Thunderbolt Attack Prana, are your go to charms for closing distance or hitting harder the combination of Heaven Thunder Hammer and Thunderbolt Attack Prana can launch people stupidly far all while closing distance.<br /> <br /> Example First Round Strike:<br /> Starting off at Medium range with 6 initiative you move to short range, then use Thunderbolt Attack Prana and Heaven Thunder Hammer this lets you zip forward again as an attack if you hit you roll 6 dice of damage which is an average of 2.4 successes doubled to 4.8 this lets you knock him a short distance into a nearby tree making him take another 4L health levels and 7B dice of damage. <br /> <br /> So he on average just took 7 bashing levels, and 4 lethal levels more than likely knocking out an Exalted without even flaring your anima unless you pumped some essence into a Brawl Excellency (Not a bad idea.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:15:16-08:00","id":776728,"title":"","content":"If you really want to emulate Saitama, try looking into the Dodge charms that let you gain initiative by evading attacks (Force-Stealing Feint, Thousand Steps' Stillness, Unbowed Willow Meditation). You might need Supernal Dodge to make it happen, but it should be possible to just spend a few turns evading strikes and then wipe someone out with one good Decisive hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 11-29-2015, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:27:53-08:00","id":776737,"title":"","content":"Semicasual, is correct as the dodge charms would make the slow build up idea better although then you would be dropping Supernal Brawl for Supernal Dodge which doesn't seem to be what you want.<br /> <br /> I would say that you don't need to go that route as a one two punch is also viable as a way to build initiative up to finish your enemy. With Ferocious Jab &amp; Fists of Iron you can easily punch through heavy armor to gather a lot of initiative. As you drop their soak by 5 and increase your damage to around 10 + successes for a good 7 initiative switch which then lets you go first with Thunderclap Rush Attack + Heaven Thunder Hammer + Thunderbolt Attack Prana, finishing the fight then and there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:31:40-08:00","id":776741,"title":"","content":"Thanks all, I'm definitely planning a lightning-speed Dodge focus. The only downside is that I might need to have weaker Stamina to truly afford the extreme levels of Dexterity and Strength I want. But I do appreciate all the suggestions! I'm definitely planning on Supernal Brawl with a side of Dodge and Athletics.<br /> <br /> ....This guy probably won't have any non-brawl/Athletics/Dodge/Integrity charms though. I've made too many subtle/utility characters who never do anything, so I'm just making a Solar who throws castles at bad people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8946-lonesome-akuma","name":"Lonesome Akuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:36:14-08:00","id":776743,"title":"","content":"Let's be real here. For for anything approaching a complete Saitama experience you need at least Essence 5, Athletics, Brawl, Dodge, and Resistance 5 and a whole bunch of Charms in each. Probably Integrity too.<br /> <br /> That said, for an actual playable, starting character, choosing either the Dodge or Resistance defensive routes work well. Brawl is pretty friendly with other Abilities - Wind and Stones Defense also increases Evasion, for instance, which goes well with Reed in the Wind increasing your Evasion cap. If you go with Supernal Dodge as your defense and use it to accumulate Initiative for a single decisive blow, I'd try to get to at least Flow Like Blood in order to do that faster.<br /> <br /> Also, Leaping Dodge Method can help you get close enough to sniper archers to employ Thunderbolt Attack Prana","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}